WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.435 --> 00:00:17.376
could see the panic on Zann's face.

2
00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:19.637
She felt a flash of fear herself.

3
00:00:20.257 --> 00:00:23.097
But then she thought again about that Shackle spell.

4
00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:27.179
"It takes magic to reverse that spell," she thought.

5
00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:32.000
"There must be some magic energy here—at least a little."

6
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.602
"Maybe they don't call it magic here," she said to Zann.

7
00:00:35.622 --> 00:00:37.603
"They might use a different word."

8
00:00:38.524 --> 00:00:40.045
She turned to face Mellis.

9
00:00:40.065 --> 00:00:42.287
"How do you create things here?

10
00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:45.449
Do you use friction or some other way?"

11
00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:49.491
"Friction?" Mellis sounded distracted.

12
00:00:49.511 --> 00:00:51.473
"I'm not sure what you mean.

13
00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:54.955
But please, tell me—what is that creature?

14
00:00:55.556 --> 00:00:57.377
I've never seen anything like it!"

15
00:00:58.137 --> 00:01:00.839
She pointed to Zing, who was sniffing at an insect.

16
00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:03.096
"That's Zing," Zann replied.

17
00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:04.377
"He's a dragon.

18
00:01:04.937 --> 00:01:06.498
I guess you don't have dragons in Terrica."

19
00:01:07.098 --> 00:01:07.858
Perda shrugged.

20
00:01:07.878 --> 00:01:11.820
"Lots of worlds don't have dragons," she reminded him.

21
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.001
"Mellis, how do you create food when you're hungry?"

22
00:01:16.082 --> 00:01:17.743
Mellis looked confused again.

23
00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:21.224
"You mean, how do I prepare it?"

24
00:01:21.744 --> 00:01:22.204
she asked.

25
00:01:22.224 --> 00:01:25.606
"I usually cook it over a fire, like everyone else.

26
00:01:26.306 --> 00:01:30.368
Although my uncle and I grow some fruits and vegetables that are edible without cooking."

27
00:01:31.116 --> 00:01:32.937
Perda and Zann traded a glance.

28
00:01:33.698 --> 00:01:35.419
Zann was looking panicky again.

29
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.982
But Perda was still thinking about that Unshackle spell.

30
00:01:39.002 --> 00:01:43.145
"I bet this world has very weak magic," she said.

31
00:01:43.165 --> 00:01:46.787
"Wyssa's home world was the same way, remember, Zann?

32
00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:53.492
That's why she learned all about mixing potions out of berries and stuff—that's how they do magic there."

33
00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:56.194
"So you think we're in Wyssa's home world?"

34
00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.115
Zann said.

35
00:01:57.875 --> 00:01:58.836
Perda shook her head.

36
00:01:59.448 --> 00:02:02.130
"This doesn't look like that world at all," she said.

37
00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:05.633
"I'm just saying that Terrica might have weak magic too."

38
00:02:06.894 --> 00:02:08.315
"Maybe," Zann agreed.

39
00:02:08.335 --> 00:02:13.460
"Come to think of it, the teachers at school are always saying that healing magic takes lots of

40
00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.802
energy. That's why they stopped letting me bring Zing to school."

41
00:02:17.623 --> 00:02:21.646
"Let's try something easier than a Healing spell," Perda said.

42
00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:24.088
"It's awfully hot out here.

43
00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:28.032
I'd like a nice, cool cup of airberry juice."

44
00:02:28.916 --> 00:02:31.077
She closed her eyes and pictured the juice.

45
00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.599
For a moment nothing happened.

46
00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:36.080
"It's not working," Zann said.

47
00:02:37.421 --> 00:02:42.944
Perda focused even harder on the image, rubbing one hand on her leg to create more friction.

48
00:02:43.544 --> 00:02:46.806
Finally she felt something land in her other hand.

49
00:02:47.286 --> 00:02:48.687
But it didn't feel like a cup.

50
00:02:49.247 --> 00:02:52.249
When she opened her eyes, it didn't look like a cup either.

51
00:02:52.789 --> 00:02:56.011
It was a single airberry, shriveled and dry.

52
00:02:56.031 --> 00:02:57.872
"Oh my goodness!"

53
00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:01.166
Mellis cried, her eyes wide with amazement.

54
00:03:01.186 --> 00:03:04.108
"You just made that berry appear out of nowhere!

55
00:03:04.749 --> 00:03:08.591
You must be nearly as powerful as Zira, the head of our village council!

56
00:03:09.632 --> 00:03:12.334
She can perform incredible feats with her potions."

57
00:03:12.354 --> 00:03:19.379
"Potions?" Perda tossed the airberry to Zing, who chomped it down eagerly.

58
00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:24.102
"Aha! That must be the only kind of magic here."

59
00:03:24.862 --> 00:03:25.643
Zann shrugged.

60
00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:26.864
"I guess so.

61
00:03:27.348 --> 00:03:31.290
At least now we know there's some magic energy in this world, even if it's not strong enough

62
00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.151
for Healing spells."

63
00:03:32.731 --> 00:03:34.372
He glanced at his scraped arm.

64
00:03:34.952 --> 00:03:36.213
Then he gasped.

65
00:03:36.233 --> 00:03:37.774
"What is it?"

66
00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.035
Perda stepped toward him, concerned.

67
00:03:40.055 --> 00:03:42.396
"Is your injury getting worse?"

68
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:44.357
"No, it's not that."

69
00:03:45.098 --> 00:03:45.818
Zann gulped.

70
00:03:45.838 --> 00:03:48.660
"The magic here isn't strong enough for Healing spells.

71
00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.702
Well, opening a wormhole takes a lot more energy than healing a scrape, doesn't it?

72
00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:54.563
What if we can't get it to open?

73
00:03:55.223 --> 00:03:56.244
How will we go home?"

74
00:03:59.036 --> 00:04:00.476
"What's a wormhole?"

75
00:04:00.897 --> 00:04:01.597
Mellis asked.

76
00:04:02.797 --> 00:04:04.257
But Perda barely heard her.

77
00:04:04.998 --> 00:04:07.658
She and Zann rushed to the spot where they'd arrived.

78
00:04:08.299 --> 00:04:12.040
The dirt and scrubby grass looked the same there as everywhere else.

79
00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.921
Luckily Perda remembered that the vortex had spit them out close to the scraggly little tree.

80
00:04:17.941 --> 00:04:20.482
"This is the spot," she told Zann.

81
00:04:20.502 --> 00:04:22.142
"I'm sure of it."

82
00:04:22.162 --> 00:04:27.124
"Back in Magica, all you have to do to open a wormhole is step close enough to it,"

83
00:04:27.544 --> 00:04:28.104
Zann said.

84
00:04:28.716 --> 00:04:32.238
"Your own natural magic energy joins with the energy in the air to open it.

85
00:04:32.879 --> 00:04:34.340
So why isn't this one opening?"

86
00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:38.403
Perda wiped sweat from her brow and glanced around.

87
00:04:38.423 --> 00:04:41.385
"Maybe I'm wrong about the spot," she said.

88
00:04:41.405 --> 00:04:43.386
"Let's try over this way."

89
00:04:44.066 --> 00:04:45.507
But no wormhole appeared.

90
00:04:45.527 --> 00:04:47.509
"The magic is weak here, right?"

91
00:04:47.929 --> 00:04:48.469
Zann said.

92
00:04:48.489 --> 00:04:51.331
"Maybe we have to create more energy to get it to open."

93
00:04:51.351 --> 00:04:54.053
"It's worth a try," Perda agreed.

94
00:04:54.674 --> 00:04:56.455
What Zann had said made sense.

95
00:04:57.155 --> 00:05:00.497
Back in Magica, magic energy was everywhere.

96
00:05:01.898 --> 00:05:05.300
Friction was a way of focusing it to do what you wanted it to do.

97
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:11.763
If the energy here was very weak, it would probably take much more friction to gather enough magic

98
00:05:11.863 --> 00:05:13.424
energy to open a wormhole.

99
00:05:14.045 --> 00:05:18.147
She and Zann spent a few minutes creating as much friction as they could.

100
00:05:18.867 --> 00:05:22.870
Zann got Zing to rub against his leg to add a little more friction.

101
00:05:25.411 --> 00:05:27.112
They even convinced Mellis to help.

102
00:05:28.252 --> 00:05:30.433
"Why are we rubbing our hands together?"

103
00:05:30.853 --> 00:05:31.893
she asked at last.

104
00:05:31.913 --> 00:05:35.434
"It's a way to bring magic energy to us," Zann explained.

105
00:05:35.454 --> 00:05:38.135
"When there's enough, the wormhole should open."

106
00:05:38.935 --> 00:05:43.216
But a short while later, their hands were sore and nothing had happened.

107
00:05:43.856 --> 00:05:47.778
"Too bad we don't have one of those relics from your parents' lab," Perda said.

108
00:05:47.798 --> 00:05:53.199
"The reason they're so powerful is that they're full of superconcentrated magic energy.

109
00:05:53.779 --> 00:05:56.220
That would definitely help us open the wormhole!"

110
00:05:57.512 --> 00:05:59.694
Zann flopped down on the ground to rest.

111
00:06:00.154 --> 00:06:01.496
Then he sat up straight.

112
00:06:01.516 --> 00:06:03.377
"Hey!" he exclaimed.

113
00:06:03.397 --> 00:06:07.280
"What about that weird metal thing we found in the Wormwood tree's root?

114
00:06:08.021 --> 00:06:09.402
It looked kind of like a relic.

115
00:06:10.063 --> 00:06:11.584
I bet that's what opened the wormhole there.

116
00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:13.686
Maybe it will work here too!"

117
00:06:14.446 --> 00:06:16.008
Perda felt a surge of hope.

118
00:06:16.588 --> 00:06:18.930
But just as quickly, her heart sank again.

119
00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.072
"Maybe," she said.

120
00:06:21.092 --> 00:06:25.996
"But I dropped it when I grabbed you to stop you from falling into the wormhole.

121
00:06:26.623 --> 00:06:28.100
It's still in Magica."
